ceo:EDTV_480p ceo:belongsToModule "TV"@en;
              a ceo:TVDisplayResolution;
              rdfs:comment """480p is the shorthand name for a video display resolution. The p stands for progressive scan, i.e. non-interlaced. The 480 denotes a vertical resolution of 480 vertically scanning lines, usually with a horizontal resolution of 640 pixels and 4:3 aspect ratio or a horizontal resolution of 854 pixels and 16:9 aspect ratio.

(This description is partly based on or reuses content from the Wikipedia article \"480p\" (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/480p) and is licensed under the GNU Free Documentation License (http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/fdl.html).)"""@en;
