        rdfs:label "PDF"@en,
                   "PDF"@de.
ceo:PDP a ceo:DisplayType;
        rdfs:comment """A plasma display panel (PDP) is a type of flat panel display common to large TV displays (37in. [940mm]). Many tiny cells between two panels of glass hold an inert mixture of noble gases. The gas in the cells is electrically turned into a plasma which then excites phosphors to emit light.

(This description is partly based on or reuses content from the Wikipedia article \"Digital newspaper technology - Plasma\" (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_newspaper_technology#Plasma) and is licensed under the GNU Free Documentation License (http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/fdl.html).)"""@en;
        rdfs:label "PDP"@en,
                   "PDP"@de.
